                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="547-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ><img id="547-1" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ><img id="547-2" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_hc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Hypercardioid" title="Hypercardioid" ><img id="547-3" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_8.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Bidirectional" title="Bidirectional" ></span>Telefunken Elektroakustik Ela M 260</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Detachable-Capsule Pencil Tube Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>Telefunken USA&#8217;s Ela M 260 is a small-diaphragm tube condenser that ships with three detachable capsules (omni, cardioid, hypercardioid) and is compatible with dozens more capsules made by other vendors (see list below).</p><p><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/telefunkenusa/elam_260_circuit.jpg" width="100" class="thumb shaft" alt="Telefunken USA Ela M 260 Circuit" />This mic is <em>not</em> a historical reproduction of the vintage Telefunken of the same name. The original Ela M 260 was manufactured by AKG for Telefunken, and used a Telefunken AC701 tube and AKG&#8217;s <a href="http://www.saturn-sound.com/Curio's/akg's_ck26_&amp;_ck28_capsules.htm">CK28</a> capsule.</p><p>The amplifier circuit was designed by AMI, which also supplies the T60 output transformer. The tube is a NOS Telefunken EF-732.</p><p>The mic ships in a padded wooden box, and includes a dedicated power supply and Gotham Audio cable, a mic clip, a shock mount, Telefunken USA&#8217;s three stock capsules, the adapter for AKG/BLUE/JZ capsules, an owner&#8217;s manual, and a fully transferable 10-year warranty.</p><p>The Telefunken USA Ela M 260 won the 2008 TEC award for Outstanding Technical Achievement in the Microphone category.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Telefunken-USA/ElaM-260">Telefunken Elektroakustik ElaM-260</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2007.</p>
